n error in MY helper, not a defect in the VI or the scratch: term_identity.new is the set of wire uids whose (source, sink)\nidentity is new after the run, which includes OLD wire uids that were re-ended by this step (23519 lost one sink to wire_remove_loose_ends at op 5;\n12150 and 31712 are pre-existing uids that gained or lost an end), so it need not equal the count of new Wire uids. In step 3 it equalled 6 only\nbecause no old wire was re-ended. Fix: gate W on the D gate (8 pairs) and record len(new) as measured (>= 7), then continue.\n\nFind the code that builds term_identity[\"new\"] (tools/stagekit.py, search term_identity) and check whether it really includes re-ended old uids.\nStrongest reason the claim is wrong; an alternative explanation (e.g. a wire that should have been deleted survived, or a duplicate wire created);\nwhat would falsify it; the cheapest discriminating test (which uids to check in tools/bench/graph_ring_p5s02c_20261010_131658.json, the base graph).\n"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DDPRizgroC8W3W2JUcqAuW","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"G:/Codes/LabVIEW_Codes/MinLab/zz_LabView VI/AAA_UNIST/2. Tracking/V6_ParallelLoop\" && mv tools/bench/diag_c164_a3_5_mkgraph.log tools/bench/diag_c164_a3_5_mkgraph_run1.log; py tools/bgrun.py --material --max-min 2 --log tools/bench/diag_c164_a3_5_mkgraph.log -- py -u tools/bench/diag_c164_a3_5_mkgraph.py >/dev/null 2>&1; grep -nE \"^GATE (PASS|FAIL) \\| [WD]|^FACT plan|^RESULT|BGRUN END\" tools/bench/diag_c164_a3_5_mkgraph.log","timeout":30000,"description":"Re-run graph-plan builder with tightened gate"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01TxRgugvDEvFcUvYV16SKLn","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"G:/Codes/LabVIEW_Codes/MinLab/zz_LabView VI/AAA_UNIST/2. Tracking/V6_ParallelLoop/tools/bench\" && sed -e 's/diag_c163_a2_2_graph_plan\\.json/diag_c164_a3_5_graph_plan.json/g' -e 's/scratch_c163_a2_2_graph_p5s02c/scratch_c164_a3_5_graph_p5s02d/g' -e 's/diag_c163_a2_2_graph\\.json/diag_c164_a3_5